##DESCRIPTION
##  Mental Math problems for subtration.
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('mental math', 'subtraction')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Integers')
## DBsection('Addition/Subtraction')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('5/3/2020')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',            'PGML.pl',
    'contextLimitedNumeric.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('LimitedNumeric');

$k1 = random(1, 3);
$b1 = 10 * random(4, 9) - $k1;
$b2 = random(12, 18);

$hun  = random(1, 5);
$ones = random(2, 5);
$a1   = $hun * 100 - $ones;
$a2   = random(130, 180);

$q = 10 * random(2, 4);

BEGIN_PGML

Answer the following addition problems using Mental math techniques.

a. [`[$b1]+[$b2]=\;`] [__]{Compute($b1 + $b2)}
b. [`[$a1]+[$a2]=\;`] [__]{Compute($a1 + $a2)}
c. [`[$q-2] + [$q-1] + [$q] + [$q+1] + [$q+2]= \;`] 
[__]{Compute(5*$q)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) In this case, notice that the first value is close to [@ 10*Round($b1/10) @], so we will use addition compensation
[``` [$b1]+[$b2] = ([$b1]+[$k1]) + ([$b2]-[$k1]) = [$b1+$k1] + [$b2-$k1] = [$b1+$b2] ```]

b) The first number is close to [$hun*100], so we will use addition compensation:
[``` [$a1] + [$a2] = ([$a1]+[$ones]) + ([$a2]-[$ones]) = [$a1+$ones] + [$a2-$ones] 
= [$a1+$a2] ```]

c) In this case, the first and fifth and 2nd and 4th add to the same value so we rearrange:

[```
\begin{aligned}
[$q-2] + [$q-1] + [$q] + [$q+1] + [$q+2] &= ([$q-2] + [$q+2]) + ([$q-1] + [$q+1]) + [$q] \\
& = [$q*2] + [$q*2] + [$q] = [$q*5]
\end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
